  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 204 AM EDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\n- Northwest Flow Regime Continues with Low Confidence for Rain\n  Chances\n\nA persistent western CONUS upper ridge and eastern CONUS upper\ntrough will keep the Great Lakes region in northwest flow with\noccasional chances for rain/thunderstorms, but low confidence on\ncoverage and QPF amounts...and perhaps similar to the under-\nperforming events from the past week.\n\nA weak shortwave trough moves through Saturday night. Not much \nmoisture available and the best lift is off to the east, so \nlow/slight chance POPs at best.\n\nAnother trough moving through late Monday into Tuesday has better\nmoisture to work with and is amplifying as it moves though, so\nhigh chance to likely POPs in NBM appear possible if not\nreminiscent of the convectively-lacking event of last Monday.\n\nThe longwave upper trough amplifies late in the week with a cold\nfront bringing another chance of rain on Friday followed by\nanother cool down for next weekend.",
